module cast_numeric.neg_7

// ONE seeded cause: a bool cast to a number -- a HELD pair, not a forbidden
// one. D54 lists no such conversion ("arbitrary types without an explicit
// rule" is its error), while its overview page spec/conversions.md ("Bool <->
// everything") gives `bool -> int` as `true=1`, and the ORACLE accepts this
// file and prints 1. The spec disagrees with itself, so novac neither compiles
// nor forbids it: the subset's refusal, until the question in
// REPORT-carina-cast.md is answered.
// NOVAC_EXPECT a bool into a number
fn main() {
    ro t = true
    println(t as u8)
}
